**Inventory overlay:** `../evidence/inventory_overlay.json`

## Target Identity and Functional Architecture

Bangkok Air keeps L'Homme's bergamot–ginger, violet-green tailoring, literal cedar, and vetiver moving under a modeled warm-climate condition. TARGET / IDEAL uses a low-vapor Paradisamide bridge; CURRENT instead uses Lemonile with restrained Hedione and Florol because the Paradisamide stock basis is unverified. It rejects Calone/Helional aquatic coding, extra clean musks, tropical-fruit prominence, and Neroli support. TARGET / IDEAL remains separate in `../candidates/LH-10.json`.

## Current-Inventory Build — Heuristic Volume Adapter

The shared child core is 4,200 µL and the controlled module is exactly 300 µL. CURRENT contains no Paradisamide; every dispensed raw stock is at least 10 µL. The 305 K headspace screen is a working model, not measured Bangkok performance.

